  <section class="umbra-hero">
    <span class="umbra-ghost" aria-hidden="true">☾</span>
    <div class="umbra-status">In active development</div>
    <h1>Umbra</h1>
    <p class="umbra-tagline">A local-first AI studio. Run, orchestrate, and audit large language models on hardware you own — with nothing leaving the machine.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="umbra-section">
    <h2>What it is</h2>
    <p>Umbra is a desktop GUI and terminal TUI for working with local models seriously: loading and switching models, orchestrating multi-step inference, inspecting what a model actually does with your prompts, and auditing runs after the fact. No cloud endpoints, no subscriptions, no telemetry — local inference is the whole product, not a fallback mode.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="umbra-section">
    <h2>Built for NVIDIA DGX Spark</h2>
    <p>Umbra is developed on and designed around <strong>NVIDIA DGX Spark</strong> — Grace Blackwell compute with 128&nbsp;GB of unified memory. That budget changes what local AI can mean: larger models resident in memory, longer contexts, and real headroom for inference auditing alongside generation. Umbra targets CUDA first and runs where CUDA runs.</p>
    <div class="umbra-pills">
      <span>NVIDIA DGX Spark</span>
      <span>CUDA-first</span>
      <span>128 GB unified memory</span>
      <span>GUI + TUI</span>
      <span>fully offline</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="umbra-section">
    <h2>Status</h2>
    <p>Umbra is in deep development at Penumbra Forge and isn't released yet. When it ships, it ships the way everything here does: open to inspection, private by default.</p>
    <p>Want to know when it's ready? Watch <a href="https://github.com/penumbraforge" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/penumbraforge</a> or write to <a href="mailto:shadoe@penumbraforge.com">shadoe@penumbraforge.com</a>.</p>
